# Code Rules

## Access Modifiers

Default to the narrowest visibility. Recommended defaults in a single-module project:

| Entity | Modifier | Note |
| --- | --- | --- |
| ViewModel | `public` (constructor `internal` when injected) | Resolved via `InjectProvider` today, will be `internal constructor` when Koin lands |
| UseCase | `internal` | Wired inside a feature, not consumed across modules |
| Repository interface | `internal` | Public API of a feature's data layer |
| Repository / DataSource impl | `internal` | Implementations are not part of the contract |
| Mapper extension function | `internal` | Free-standing `fun ApolloType.toDomain(): DomainType` |
| Composable Screen | `internal` | Entry point for a navigation route |
| Composable View | `internal` | Re-used inside a feature |
| Preview composable | `private` | Never leaks |
| UI ViewState / Action / Event | `public` | Forms part of the ViewModel contract |
| Local JSON model (`Hero`, `Item`, `Ability`) | `public` | Used across features |
| `BaseViewModel` itself | `abstract` | In `base/` package, no further restriction |

When multi-module split lands, revisit this — features will expose only `api` types as `public`.

## Member Ordering

```kotlin
class SomeFeatureViewModel {
    // 1. companion object — top, when present and used as namespace for constants
    // 2. Properties (private MutableStateFlows / dependencies)
    // 3. init blocks
    // 4. override methods (e.g., obtainEvent)
    // 5. public functions (none for a ViewModel — UI uses obtainEvent)
    // 6. internal functions
    // 7. private functions
}
```

Companion objects holding only constants may also sit at the bottom — pick one style per file and stay consistent.

## NPE-safety

- Forbid `!!`. If you cannot recover from null, throw `IllegalStateException("explanation")` explicitly.
- Forbid `list.first()` / `list.last()` when emptiness is plausible. Use `firstOrNull()` / `lastOrNull()` / `getOrNull(index)`.
- Apollo-generated types can have nullable fields; do not unwrap them with `!!` — handle `null` in the mapper.
- `String?` defaults: prefer `.orEmpty()` over `?: ""` for readability.

## Composables

- `Modifier` is the first optional parameter and default `Modifier`.
- No business logic in composables — delegate to ViewModel via `obtainEvent`.
- `@Composable` functions are never `suspend`.

## Comments

Default: no comments. Only add when the *why* is non-obvious (a hidden invariant, a workaround for an SDK bug, a reason that diverges from the rule). Never narrate what the code does — names already do that.
